Why Are Semiconductor Pellicles Becoming Important in Advanced Lithography?

Photomasks play an essential role in transferring circuit patterns onto semiconductor wafers. Maintaining their cleanliness is important because contamination can affect the quality of transferred patterns and potentially reduce production yields.

Semiconductor pellicles provide a protective barrier over photomasks, helping keep particles away from the critical pattern plane. Their optical properties also need to support the exposure requirements of the lithography process.

As semiconductor manufacturers adopt more advanced manufacturing nodes, pellicle performance becomes increasingly important. Manufacturers must balance protection, optical transmission, thermal stability and mechanical reliability.

The need for consistent contamination control is therefore a major factor supporting the continued relevance of pellicle technology.

